# Audio / bot-state

Per-guild in-memory state only (`BotStateManager` → `Map<guildId, BotState>`). One queue, player, and `playAttempt` per guild. Lost on restart — do not add persistence or cross-guild sharing without an explicit design change.

## Playback flow

```
/play → enqueue → join VC → PlayAttempt → yt-dlp buffer → optional ffmpeg pitch → audioPlayer.play
```

Idle with `attempt.isPlaying` dequeues head and advances (or schedules 30‑min leave).

## Invariants — do not break

- **Guild isolation**: all ops keyed by `guildId`; never share players across guilds
- **PlayAttempt races**: after download/pitch/awaits, re-check validity before `audioPlayer.play()`; always `cancel()` (kill yt-dlp) when clearing/replacing
- **Idle-only dequeue** for committed audio; player `error` must not dequeue
- **Skip**: stop player when it owns a resource; Idle + in-flight download uses cancel + slice
- **Start playback** only when enqueueing into an empty queue
- **Full-buffer media**: entire track buffered (then optionally pitch-shifted) before play

## Where to edit

Prefer race logic in `audio-play-guard.ts` plus `test/audio/audio-play-guard.test.js` over scattering checks in `AudioManager`. Handlers in `api/routes/audio-routes.ts` stay thin wrappers.
